---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { profile } from "../data/profile";
---
<BaseLayout title="About Arman Mishra | Enkidu" description="About Arman Mishra, penetration tester and security researcher.">
  <section class="page-hero container">
    <div class="eyebrow">ABOUT / THE PERSON BEHIND THE TERMINAL</div>
    <h1>Arman Mishra<span class="hero-accent">Known online as Enkidu.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">A penetration tester and security researcher interested in understanding systems beyond their surface-level behaviour.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container content-layout section">
    <aside class="side-note">
      <span>FIELD NOTE / 001</span>
      <strong>Think before exploiting.</strong>
      <p>Enumeration is not a formality. It is where understanding begins.</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <p>I’m Arman Mishra, known online as Enkidu. I’m pursuing a Bachelor of Computer Applications with a specialization in Cyber Security at Lovely Professional University, with expected graduation in 2028.</p>
      <p>My work and interests span web application security, network penetration testing, Windows and Linux security, and Active Directory. I enjoy understanding how systems behave, how trust boundaries are formed, and how weaknesses can connect into meaningful attack paths.</p>
      <h2>How I approach security</h2>
      <p>I put enumeration before exploitation. A service banner, an authentication prompt, a group membership, or a promising lead is not automatically proof of impact. I prefer to build a hypothesis from evidence, test it with a discriminating check, and document what the results actually demonstrate.</p>
      <p>Alongside practical testing, I build tools such as Shredder and Ink, develop CTF challenges, and create lab environments to understand offensive techniques from the ground up.</p>
      <h2>What I’m building towards</h2>
      <p>My immediate goal is to grow through security research, practical assessments, meaningful projects, and an internship opportunity. Over the longer term, I want to deepen my work in red-team operations and security research.</p>
      <p class="signature">— Arman / Enkidu</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
